# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING DATA-SHAPED ENTERS THIS REPOSITORY.
#
# The generated files here are synthetic and harmless, and they are still
# gitignored. Two reasons:
#
#   1. A repo that never contains data files cannot accidentally contain a
#      real one. The habit is the protection, not the judgment call each time.
#   2. Synthetic data is reproducible from the generator plus a seed. Committing
#      it stores megabytes to preserve something one command regenerates, and
#      guarantees that the committed copy eventually disagrees with the code.
#
# Ship the generator, not the output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
example/_data/
example/_output/

*.csv
*.csv.gz
*.sas7bdat
*.parquet
*.fst
*.dta
*.rds
*.RData

# Exception: small public reference tables that belong under version control.
# references/ holds dated copies of the CMS inputs a generator depends on —
# they are public documents, not data, and a pipeline built this way needs them.
!templates/*.csv
!references/*.csv
!references/*.xlsx

# Claude Code working files.
# CLAUDE.md is a symlink into Dropbox (_vrdc_shared/_claude/). It holds private
# working notes and machine paths, and this repo is going public.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/

.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.DS_Store
slides/*.aux
slides/*.log
slides/*.nav
slides/*.out
slides/*.snm
slides/*.toc
slides/*.vrb

# Private worklog — lives in Dropbox (_vrdc_shared/_claude/), never in git.
worklog.md
*_worklog.md

# LaTeX editor sync files
*.synctex.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local working material, not part of the published blueprint.
#
# These stay on disk and remain fully runnable on a working copy; git simply
# does not track them. Note that a clone will not have them, so anything here
# must never become a dependency of the published material.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
example/
R/read_data.R
R/era.R
docs/03-era-harmonization.md
docs/07-ai-assisted-development.md
docs/08-bootstrap-checklist.md
R/qc_report.R
